**Flexible location:** With locations across multiple regions, the successful candidate may be based in the **Quebec City, Sherbrooke, or Montreal South Shore area**.
Major manufacturing transformations require a clear vision, sound decisions, and the ability to evolve practices across an organization.


As **Director, Manufacturing \& Engineering Practice**, you will serve as a strategic and technical partner to the Chief Manufacturing Officer and play a key role in advancing operations across Innovair Solutions.


You will define the direction, standards, and roadmaps for manufacturing excellence, industrial engineering, automation, and operational transformation. Through your influential leadership, you will help align practices across our various sites, accelerate innovation, and drive sustainable improvements in manufacturing performance.


You will also support the Group’s growth by contributing to strategic investment projects as well as the assessment and integration of new acquisitions.


If you are looking to bring your vision, manufacturing expertise, and ability to influence to a growing organization where transformation comes to life on the shop floor, we would love to meet you.

**In this strategic role, you will be responsible for:**

* Defining the corporate vision and roadmap for industrial engineering, operational excellence, and manufacturing transformation;
* Acting as a strategic partner to the Chief Manufacturing Officer in establishing manufacturing priorities, investments, and strategic direction;
* Ensuring alignment and standardization of manufacturing practices across business units and production sites;
* Developing and leading the strategy for automation, robotics, and the digital transformation of operations;
* Monitoring technological developments and identifying emerging technologies, manufacturing methods, and solutions that can enhance the Group’s competitiveness;
* Contributing to the prioritization of the strategic manufacturing project portfolio and evaluating major **CAPEX investments**, including their relevance, expected benefits, and return on investment;
* Contributing to **mergers and acquisitions (M\&A)** activities by assessing manufacturing capabilities, technologies, operational risks, and potential synergies, and supporting the integration of acquired businesses;
* Advancing operational excellence by deploying **Lean Manufacturing**, continuous improvement, standardization, and health and safety optimization principles;
* Identifying opportunities to improve productivity, quality, costs, lead times, and manufacturing capacity;
* Establishing and monitoring manufacturing performance indicators to measure the value generated by various initiatives;
* Providing functional leadership to industrial engineering teams across multiple sites while promoting knowledge sharing, skills development, and best practices.




This position does not have direct management responsibility for plant industrial engineering teams. Rather, it provides functional leadership across the Group to ensure consistency, standardization, and continuous advancement of practices.

 **What will contribute to your success in this role:**


* Bachelor’s degree in industrial, mechanical, electrical, manufacturing engineering, or a related field;
* Member in good standing of the **Ordre des ingénieurs du Québec (OIQ)**;
* Minimum of **15 years of experience in a manufacturing environment**, including at least **10 years in a leadership role**;
* Significant experience in continuous improvement, operational excellence, and manufacturing transformation;
* Strong knowledge of **Lean Manufacturing** principles and manufacturing performance management;
* Experience managing **CAPEX investment projects**, automation, and robotics initiatives;
* Experience in a **growing, multisite manufacturing environment**, including integration or organizational transformation projects;
* Strong knowledge of **Industry 4\.0 technologies** and digital transformation;
* Strong influencing, mobilization, and leadership skills in a matrix organization;
* Knowledge of emerging metal transformation technologies considered an asset;
* Proficiency with the Microsoft Office suite;
* Advanced proficiency in both French and English, written and spoken, to meet the requirements of the role and interact effectively with various stakeholders.
* **Travel required (approximately 30% of the time):** Must be able to travel to the company’s various sites in Canada and internationally, based on business needs. Must be eligible to travel and hold all required documentation for business travel.

**The advantages of being part of our team:**


This strategic role will give you the opportunity to **help shape the evolution of our manufacturing network**, lead large\-scale initiatives, and have a lasting influence on our organization. You will benefit from a high degree of flexibility, distinctive working conditions, and the opportunity to make a tangible impact in an agile, people\-focused, and collaborative environment.


* Profit\-sharing program;
* Flexible work schedule;
* Remote work;
* Group insurance plan with employer contribution, available from your first day;
* Employee and Family Assistance Program;
* Telemedicine services;
* Retirement plan with employer contributions;
* Personal days;
* Employee and family discounts on select products.





Message from the Recruiters  



We can’t wait to meet you!  



Because we’re passionate about people, we’re eager to learn about your aspirations and see how your potential can flourish with us.  



Want to learn more about the opportunities that could be waiting for you? We’re looking forward to your application!  



